Z||000000||KRMFiero||11-20-2000||04:02 PM||||Okay here goes:<BR>While my Fiero does not run what things should i save for... I want to get a sunroof off a fiero, how easy is this for a teenager? also interested in a fastback conversion, should i do this? again how easy is this to do? Interior... I ordered white guage stickers but what are some other things that will make it look more "different"? Engine... I want to eather keep with a L4 though i will need to get a new one but the 350 conversion from archie  if that comes with every nut and bolt and will pass inspection i would be interested in that<P>also how hard is it to change bumper covers? what would look nice and "dfferent"?<P>Does anyone know any places that sell the sunroof conversion as a kit and possibly the fastback conversion as a kit so i dont have to search for a donor?<P>thanx||||reg||5
Z||000001||Will||11-20-2000||08:21 PM||||All Fieros have the necessary hole in the chassis roof to have a sunroof installed. Installing one is simply a matter of removing the outer roof panel and headliner and installing the outer roof panel and headliner (and sunroof) from a sunroof-equiped car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||11-20-2000||11:11 PM||||I'm not sure what year coupe you have but I like the 87-88 coupe bumper covers. They're pretty easy to interchange. The fastback conversion is easy if you take your time and make sure you have all the bolts out and that you don't bust up the roof panel when removing and replacing the clip.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||11-20-2000||11:18 PM||||hell, just buy a 86-88 gt.  it might cost you more in the long run to keep your car and do all the mods you want.  i was thinking about changin my coupe into a 85gt look, but it was gonna cost me too much.  i figured i'll just find a cheap fiero that already has what i want.<P>well it may not have helped, but there's my 3 cents.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||10
Z||000004||RaeQwan||11-21-2000||12:58 AM||||Not bashing you or anything, (sparkie plug-dont ask, I dont know), but isn't part of the fun of owning a Fiero the fact of making them our own? customizing them, enjoying the hella out of doing the customization? I hate doing custom work, but enjoy the hella out of doing. hehe. Me & my car have a love/hate relationship, as long as I love the devil out of it(bad devil), it wont hate me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwancfa.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||2xsess||11-21-2000||07:31 AM||||Here's one that I think looks pretty nice  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> If I ever get an 87-88 coupe I might do this.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fastback_with_coupe_nose_2.jpg"> <P>I agree with RaeQwan making your Fiero personalized is the best part of it. Might not be a whole lot of fun while you're doing it but when it's done you can sit back and say, I did that.||||reg||1
